WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.830
In 1991, about 31 in every 100
jobs in the UK were in industry.

2
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:10.330
By 2023, it was about 16.

3
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:14.690
Meanwhile, more than 8 in
10 UK jobs were in services.

4
00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.310
So why do most workers
in rich countries never

5
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:19.640
make anything you can touch?

6
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.990
In this mission, you'll
follow a loaf of bread

7
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.680
from the field to the shop,

8
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.020
through three sectors of the economy.

9
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.350
Then you'll read real data on jobs,

10
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:32.120
and compare countries where
most people still work on farms.

11
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:36.200
Your mission: find out why
rich economies run on services,

12
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.610
and what that means
for the jobs people do.
